# Logs
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local

# Environment. `*.local` above already covers .env.local, but not .env or
# .env.production — and SUBSCRIBE_TOKEN is a credential. The example file is
# the one that is meant to be committed: it carries names, never values.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Next.js
.next
/out
next-env.d.ts
*.tsbuildinfo

# `next dev` writes these on every run — rules files for AI agents, generated
# from next.config rather than authored. Regenerated on demand, so they are not
# the repository's to carry. `agentRules: false` in next.config turns them off
# entirely if they are ever unwanted locally too.
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md

# Bytecode from app/hero/generate-scene.py.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

# Deliberately not committed. npm on macOS records the linux-musl `sharp`
# binaries (an optional dependency of Next) with no version, which is harmless
# locally but makes `npm install` fail on Vercel's Linux builders with
# "Invalid Version:". Letting the deploy resolve its own tree avoids it.
# Trade-off: installs are no longer pinned. Commit a lockfile generated on
# Linux if reproducible builds become important.
package-lock.json
